    "note": "Senate Draft 2 (carried-over heading shows H.D. 2 and S.D. 2). The first quoted item stops at \"rounds\" because the struck words \"which are designed for or capable of use with a pistol\" follow; the proviso then lists exceptions. The penalty for a magazine violation (misdemeanor, class C felony if inserted in a firearm) and SECTION 2 and 4 (film-prop permit and exemption for magazines over ten rounds) are not quoted because they cross struck words. Passage votes exist; amendments after SD2 are not in the text read."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 3 (HRS 134-8): The manufacture, possession, sale, barter, trade, gift, transfer, or acquisition of detachable ammunition magazines with a capacity in excess of ten rounds\nSECTION 3 (HRS 134-8): (1) Possessed by a person who legally possessed the magazine prior to the effective date of Act ;\nSECTION 3 (HRS 134-8): (2) Acquired by a person by means of inheritance from another person who legally possessed the magazine prior to the effective date of Act ;\nSECTION 3 (HRS 134-8): (3) Acquired, possessed, and used by a law enforcement agency or duly authorized law enforcement officer for official purposes.\nSECTION 3 (HRS 134-8): Any person violating subsection (a) or (b) shall be guilty of a class C felony and shall be imprisoned for a term of five years without probation."
}